From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:30:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: skip unpublished stations in the station
 poll

mt7915_mac_sta_poll() takes a station off the poll list under
sta_poll_lock and uses it after dropping the lock. Removal only unlinks
it from that list, so if the station had already been unpublished, the
RCU read section held by the poll doesn't keep it alive. Only process
stations whose wcid is still published when they are taken off the
list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index c5b37ee5..03041106 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ static void mt7915_mac_sta_poll(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 	rcu_read_lock();
 
 	while (true) {
-		bool clear = false;
+		bool clear = false, published;
 		u32 addr, val;
 		u16 idx;
 		s8 rssi[4];
@@ -123,9 +123,19 @@ static void mt7915_mac_sta_poll(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 		msta = list_first_entry(&sta_poll_list,
 					struct mt7915_sta, wcid.poll_list);
 		list_del_init(&msta->wcid.poll_list);
+		idx = msta->wcid.idx;
+		/*
+		 * Removal unlinks poll_list under this lock, so msta is alive
+		 * here. If its wcid is still published, the synchronize_net()
+		 * that precedes the free has to wait for our rcu_read_lock();
+		 * otherwise removal may complete while we use msta below.
+		 */
+		published = rcu_access_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[idx]) ==
+			    &msta->wcid;
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 
-		idx = msta->wcid.idx;
+		if (!published)
+			continue;
 
 		/* refresh peer's airtime reporting */
 		addr = mt7915_mac_wtbl_lmac_addr(dev, idx, 20);
